{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "growth_lr2m_tracer_D_bin_closed",
    "description": "Companion of growth_lr2m_D_bin_closed for any quantity carried by the particles' VOLUME -- component masses, aerosol water, a dry-volume tracer -- on the trailing axis `tracer`: the consumer writes dm/dt = -D(lam*m, N, V, wrt: bin) + ... with m [cell, bin, tracer] and the section number N and dry volume V [cell, bin] as trailing operands (esm-spec 9.6.8). The particles crossing an edge each carry the edge volume, and m is uniformly mixed over its donor section's volume, so the flux of m through an edge is v_edge F_N m_donor/V_donor, with F_N the number flux of growth_lr2m_D_bin_closed (sectional_lr2m_tracer_flux_up / _down). That is MOSAIC's apply_moves, which moves every component and the water by the same volume fraction xferfracvol, in the dt -> 0 limit. Telescoping per tracer (sum_j dm_j/dt = 0), closed at both ends of the size range exactly as the number rule. The arity (three operands) keeps the two rules disjoint: the number rule's two-operand pattern cannot match this node, nor this pattern that one. Second order on smooth data, as the number rule whose number flux it carries (measured with it on problems/growth_sectional_lr2m_mms). Requires NBIN >= 2.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:sectional_volume_1d",
      "op:advection",
      "order:2",
      "scheme:linear-discrete",
      "scheme:upwind",
      "bc:closed",
      "form:flux",
      "spec:9.6.8",
      "axes:cell,bin,tracer"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R. A., Easter, R. C., Fast, J. D., & Peters, L. K. (2008). Model for Simulating Aerosol Interactions and Chemistry (MOSAIC). Journal of Geophysical Research, 113, D13204.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2007JD008782"
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF-Chem v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_movesect.F, subroutines move_sections_calc_masnumadvect and move_sections_apply_moves (R. C. Easter), the 'linear-discrete' / mass-number-advection section-moving algorithm (msectional = 20)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Gelbard, F., Tambour, Y., & Seinfeld, J. H. (1980). Sectional representations for simulating aerosol dynamics. Journal of Colloid and Interface Science, 76(2), 541-556.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9797(80)90394-X"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/sectional_lr2m_growth_tracer_interior.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/sectional_lr2m_tracer_flux_up.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/sectional_lr2m_tracer_flux_down.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
